%
% Probabilistic marginal under a declared DEPENDENCY model (#506).
% a and b are perfectly correlated by the explicit joint table:
%   joint(0.5, a, b)   — both true with probability 0.5
%   joint(0.5)         — neither true with probability 0.5
% The rule both :- a, b makes `both` derivable only when a AND b hold, so
%   P(both) = 0.5  (the joint mass of the (a∧b) outcome).
% Under a (wrong) independence reading this would be 0.5·0.5 = 0.25 — the
% differing value proves the declared joint is used.
% Expected: X = ex:on with probability 0.5, status ok.
:- prefix(ex, 'https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-dependency-joint/').
:- probability_model(dependency).
:- joint(0.5, ex:a(ex:s, ex:on), ex:b(ex:s, ex:on)).
:- joint(0.5).
ex:both(S, ex:on) :- ex:a(S, ex:on), ex:b(S, ex:on).
?- ex:both(ex:s, X).
